# Frontend Next.js Rules

## Stack
- Next.js 15+ App Router
- TypeScript

## Conventions
- Routes under `app/`.
- Shared API client in `lib/api.ts`.
- Reusable UI in `components/`.

## UX Requirements
- All forms have validation and disabled/loading states.
- Empty, loading, and error states required for each page.
- Keep copy specific and action-oriented.

## Data Contracts
- Frontend types mirror documented API payloads.
- Do not invent fields unsupported by backend.

## Testing
- At least one UI test for core order flow and one unit test for form validation logic.
